  "title": "French Blood Storage Impacted by Freezer Hacks",
  "summary": "Hundreds of French blood storage facilities were targeted by hackers, causing food spoilage, fires, and significant financial losses, as reported by The Guardian World and BBC World News. A second cyberattack targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in Europe led to similar incidents, with temperatures reaching up to 50°C in some cases.",
  "facts": [
