      "title": "French blood banks hacked in latest cyber-attack on Europe",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/04/france-national-blood-service-hack-cyber-attack-europe",
      "description": "<p>Temperature and defrosting thresholds raised to ‘very high levels’ at three cold stores stocking vital blood products</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/04/eu-ukraine-russia-france-germany-us-nato-europe-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>France’s national blood service has said hackers accessed control systems and boosted temperatures at three cold stores stocking vital blood products, in an apparent escalation of recent cyber-attacks on fridges and freezers across Europe.</p><p><a href=\"https://presse.efs.sante.fr/actualites/l-efs-confirme-l-incident-de-cybersecurite-impactant-un-de-ces-prestataires-d-equipement-frigorifique-2c07c-08a0a.html\">The French blood service (EFS) said</a> temperature and defrosting thresholds had been raised to “very high levels” in the attack, adding that its alarm systems had allowed technicians to intervene before the products were compromised.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/04/france-national-blood-service-hack-cyber-attack-europe\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
